    'without sustained vomiting or inability to pass flatus. She reports two to three nonbloody stools per day. Her recent\n'
    'hemoglobin was 10.6 g/dL with ferritin 12 ng/mL despite oral iron; fecal calprotectin was mildly elevated. There is\n'
    'no current fever, overt gastrointestinal hemorrhage, or unintentional rapid weight loss.\n'
    'MR enterography performed September 21, 2026 demonstrated a short, fixed narrowing at the ileocolonic\n'
    'anastomosis with modest upstream neo-terminal ileal caliber change and without an abscess, fistula, phlegmon, or\n'
    'high-grade obstruction. The narrowing was estimated at approximately 1 cm in length. The multidisciplinary IBD\n'
    'service considered a trial of endoscopic balloon dilation reasonable, provided the endoscopic appearance showed no\n'
    'deep ulceration or suspicion for malignancy. The examination was also requested for dysplasia surveillance given the\n'
    'duration of colonic involvement and a remote history of an inflammatory polyp.\n'
    'Pertinent records reviewed before the examination\n'
    'A colonoscopy from January 2024 described a patent but narrowed ileocolonic anastomosis, mild neo-terminal ileal\n'
    'ulceration, and a 4 mm rectal hyperplastic polyp that was removed at that earlier encounter. No dilation was carried\n'
    'out in 2024. An outside upper endoscopy performed in March 2023 documented a Schatzki ring treated with\n'
    'balloon dilation and gastric biopsies at that time. Those upper gastrointestinal interventions are historical only; no\n'
    'esophagogastroduodenoscopy or other upper endoscopic procedure was performed on November 8, 2026.\n'
    'Available prior pathology did not document dysplasia. The present report records only the lower gastrointestinal\n'
